  "estimateLimits": [
    "Logical RGBA8 decoded/backing and complete GPU mip estimates, not measured process RSS or driver allocation.",
    "Geometry GPU total assumes every listed mesh is uploaded; CPU arrays are retained by full constructors even if frustum-culled.",
    "Excludes browser overhead, shader/compiler temporary memory, shadows, cloud render targets/PMREM, swash, rock images and geometry, worker temporaries and forest."
  ],
  "visualConfounds": [
    "Removing forest removes real reflected canopy silhouettes/color and its sun shadows; nearshore roughness judgments would see different incident radiance.",
    "Forcing existing far atlases changes nearby geometry/coverage; palms have no existing far-atlas branch. Three atlas sets alone add a significant retained/derived texture budget.",
    "Cropping geometry needs the reflected view and shadow casters too, while ocean bathymetry explicitly depends on the full continuation. It is not a drop-in camera crop.",
    "Downsampling sand normal/ARM changes exactly the gloss/grain response under review; downsampling albedo also needs linear-light filtering to preserve calibration.",
    "Rock geometry-only pack preserves collision positions/indices but omits the scan normal/UV/PBR images; it cannot replace the visible source without a declared shading approximation."
  ],
  "usefulness": "An aggressively bounded variant could test shoreline coordinate/contact faults, but cannot decide production sand appearance or forest reflection quality. Existing actual-plane GPU fixture already establishes the optics plumbing; the full-scene matrix remains the useful next visual gate.",
